# Drafted by Gemini (R13 gate), edited.

~ start
if not quest.fields_of_the_crow >= gate
quest fields_of_the_crow gate
endif
Narrator: A wall of dry corn rises ahead, smelling of dust and old feathers. Two amber eyes with star-shaped pupils blink open among the husks.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens. A wall of corn with a doorman. I'd grade the workmanship highly.
raum [sly]: Nobody walks my rows for free, little birds. Drop a secret in my beak, something real and sour, and I will part the stalks.
* Pay a secret of my own -> own
* [if flag.secret_martha] Pay Martha Langtree's secret -> other_martha
* [if flag.secret_jonah] Pay Jonah Sawyer's secret -> other_jonah
* [if flag.secret_isaac] Pay Isaac Langtree's secret -> other_isaac
* [if flag.secret_william] Pay William Lodge's secret -> other_william
* Not yet -> not_yet

~ own
approve rook_coldwake +2 tobin_hayward +2 silas_vane -2: You paid the crow's toll with your own secret
Narrator: You speak a shameful truth you never meant another soul to hear. A crow drops from the stalks and plucks a dark feather from your shoulder that was never a feather at all.
raum [smile]: Sweet and rotten to the core. Keep that little shame warm for me, traveller, I will come collect the rest by and by.
interject name:silas_vane: Never sign an open tab with a bird that eats the ledger, friend.
set paid_own_secret
set secrets_paid += 1
set maze_open
-> END

~ other_martha
approve silas_vane +2 rook_coldwake -2 tobin_hayward -2: You spent Martha Langtree's secret to pass the corn wall
raum [smile]: Old Martha keeping that dry husk in the dark while she curses her neighbour. That is a heavy coin, and it spends just fine.
Narrator: Far back toward the burning square, Martha Langtree stops mid-sentence, her hand flying to her throat as the corn parts before you.
set told_raum_martha
set secrets_paid += 1
set maze_open
-> END

~ other_jonah
approve silas_vane +2 rook_coldwake -2 tobin_hayward -2: You spent Jonah Sawyer's secret to open the corn maze
raum [smile]: Young Jonah playing with matches and crying over the ashes. I can taste the soot on his tongue from here.
Narrator: The dry leaves shiver with a sound like a boy gasping for air, and the woven stalks untangle to clear the path.
set told_raum_jonah
set secrets_paid += 1
set maze_open
-> END

~ other_isaac
approve silas_vane +2 rook_coldwake -3: You traded a dead man's confession to the crow king
raum [sly]: Poor dead Isaac, folded up in the cellar chest like winter linen. Even the quiet ones have a little marrow left in them.
Narrator: A cold draft smells briefly of cedarwood and old wool as the tall stalks draw back on either side.
set told_raum_isaac
set secrets_paid += 1
set maze_open
-> END

~ other_william
raum [smile]: Decent William Lodge, carrying a weight he never set down on the road from Wickermoor. Stolen grain tastes sweetest of all.
Narrator: Near the wagons, a horse stamps once in the dirt, and the wall of corn splits open with a dry, rasping sigh.
set told_raum_william
set secrets_paid += 1
set maze_open
-> END

~ not_yet
raum [weary]: Cluck your tongues and keep your lockboxes shut, then. The rows will wait until the fire drives you back.
-> END
